## Anthropic PDF functional reference — restricted source not incorporated

Sources consulted:

- <https://github.com/K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills/tree/b2a92ba052dcae4ef48e850b9e31ebf75706be48/skills/pdf>
- <https://github.com/anthropics/skills/tree/f6656c1256d5a8adfa37db9110046ef20bac644c/skills/pdf>

K-Dense repository commit consulted:
`b2a92ba052dcae4ef48e850b9e31ebf75706be48` (2026-08-14). The PDF
skill identifies metadata version `1.2`, Anthropic as the author, and the
Anthropic repository as its source. Anthropic repository commit
`f6656c1256d5a8adfa37db9110046ef20bac644c` was also consulted on
2026-08-14.

The source skill's own `LICENSE.txt` is not MIT: it governs use through the
applicable Anthropic services agreement and states additional restrictions on
copying, retention, derivative works, distribution, transfer, and reverse
engineering. Those materials were reviewed only to identify the public
functional surface of a PDF capability. No source prose, script, fixture,
asset, form guide, reference guide, or license text was copied, translated,
vendored, or adapted into this repository.

`skills/tool/q-tool-pdf` is an original Quasar implementation. It covers the
same public functional area with an independently designed caller-owned
delegation contract, operation-aware Python/Node routing,
source-preserving atomic output, explicit overwrite authorization, native-tool
security boundaries, runtime-specific references, and deterministic smoke
tests. Original Quasar portions remain under the repository MIT license above;
third-party runtime dependencies retain their own licenses and are not
vendored.

## K-Dense Inc. adaptations — MIT License

Source repository: <https://github.com/K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills>

Commit consulted: `13385c7c4db02fdcc84a020752c07cce91ef780e`
(2026-08-13). The source repository uses `LICENSE.md`; the source skill
frontmatter also declares MIT.

| Source skill | Quasar scope and modifications |
|---|---|
| `skills/scientific-brainstorming` (metadata version `1.1`) | `skills/ideation/q-ideation-session/scripts/_common.py`, `session_scaffold.py`, `validate_register.py`, and `evaluate_matrix.py`; `references/method-core.md`, `evaluation-and-gates.md`, `responsible-ai.md`, and `sources.md`. Quasar generalized scientific ideas to profile-scoped candidates, replaced literature search with typed handoffs, added decision and information governance, and retained scientific gates only in the scientific profile. The register schema, baseline freeze, profile references, and handoffs are original Quasar work. |
| `skills/market-research-reports` (metadata version `1.2`) | `skills/research/q-research-market-analysis/SKILL.md`; `references/measurement-and-sizing.md`, `forecast-and-sensitivity.md`, `competitor-and-concentration.md`, and `methods-and-ethics.md`; `scripts/_common.py`, `calculate_market_sizing.py`, `forecast_sensitivity.py`, `check_unit_consistency.py`, and `validate_competitor_matrix.py`. Quasar replaced upstream ledgers and report scaffolds with Quasar IDs and owners, removed source acquisition and participant operations, and added bounded offline validation, calculation lineage, and single-writer limits. The market-analysis schema, custom methods, concentration calculator, tests, fixtures, and example are original Quasar work. |
| `skills/scientific-critical-thinking` (metadata version `1.2`) | `skills/review/q-review-evidence/SKILL.md` and its five files under `references/`. Quasar rewrote selected appraisal concepts as a bounded, read-only business, engineering, scientific, or clinical evidence diagnostic; added claim-fit and caller-ownership rules; and made detailed lenses conditional. Invocation metadata is original Quasar work. |

